.el .ds Aq '
.TH tapectl-library 1  "tapectl-library " 
.SH NAME
tapectl\-library \- Manage media libraries (folder=unit factory + batch tape driver)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtapectl library\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage media libraries (folder=unit factory + batch tape driver)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output in JSON format
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be done without making changes
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose output
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip confirmation prompts
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to config file
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
tapectl\-library\-sync(1)
Sync every configured library: register new unit folders, resolve moved/renamed ones by dotfile uuid, mark vanished ones `missing` (never deleted or retired — those are operator acts)
.TP
tapectl\-library\-status(1)
Show pending/dirty/missing/under\-copied counts for every configured library
.TP
tapectl\-library\-plan(1)
Show the batch plan (alphabetical first\-fit, §7) for every configured library\*(Aqs pending units
.TP
tapectl\-library\-run(1)
Execute one batch: stage every unit in it once, write one session per destination label, then release staging. Targets a single library (unlike `sync`/`status`/`plan`, which sweep every configured library) since a batch write is a real, one\-shot tape action
.TP
tapectl\-library\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
